      <p>If the opener light blinks and the door reverses when you try to close it, the photo eye sensors are likely misaligned or blocked. These sensors are mounted on either side of the door near the floor and must "see" each other for the door to close. Check for obstructions, dirt on the sensor lens, or sensors that have been bumped out of alignment. If the sensors look clear and aligned, the issue might be a faulty sensor, loose wiring, or a circuit board problem requiring professional repair.</p>
